# Cursor Rules for This Repository (AutoAnalyst)

## Project Overview
- App goal: Automatically analyze uploaded tabular datasets and present EDA + ML results in an interactive dashboard.
- Audience: data analysts, learners, and developers needing rapid insight generation.
- Status: active development prototype (not production finalized).

## Stack and Dependencies
- Python backend with FastAPI.
- Data/ML stack: pandas, numpy, scipy, scikit-learn.
- Single-file frontend: dashboard.html (vanilla JS + CSS).
- CDN dependencies in frontend: Chart.js, PapaParse, Google Fonts.
- sqlite metadata persistence and optional bearer auth are configured; no cloud services are configured.

## Source Layout
- main.py: API entrypoint, CORS config, endpoint handlers, in-memory session store.
- ingestion.py: upload parsing and schema/type normalization.
- eda_engine.py: EDA computations (stats/distributions/correlations/anomalies/KPIs).
- modeling.py: model task detection, feature prep, training, generated insights.
- dashboard.html: complete UI shell, local state, rendering functions, upload/model calls.
- README.md: concept docs, but file/folder map differs from current workspace state.

## Completed Functionality
- End-to-end upload -> EDA -> display path is implemented.
- Baseline ML retraining by selected target column is implemented.
- Demo mode works without backend by computing local EDA/model placeholder logic.
- Correlation heatmap, distribution charts, anomaly cards, model metrics, and raw data preview are implemented.

## Pending Functionality / Risks
- Add persistent storage/session durability.
- Add tests (unit + integration).
- Add auth/security/file-size constraints and tighten CORS.
- Use backend scatter/column endpoints consistently for richer explorer behavior.
- Improve production readiness (dependency pinning, deployment config, monitoring).

## Coding Conventions to Follow
- Python:
  - snake_case names.
  - Keep endpoint JSON payloads explicit and serializable.
  - Preserve current run_eda/run_modeling contract shape unless frontend updates in same change.
- Frontend JS:
  - Keep STATE as canonical client state.
  - Use small renderX() functions that update isolated DOM sections.
  - Keep API requests via fetch + async/await.
- CSS:
  - Preserve token-based :root variables and existing visual language.
  - Prefer semantic class names over utility proliferation.

## Error Handling Norms
- Backend: use HTTPException for expected validation/session errors; catch and return controlled 500 for unexpected exceptions.
- Frontend: show user-friendly UI error for upload/model failures; avoid silent failures.

## Important Notes
- API base is hardcoded to http://localhost:8000 in dashboard.html.
- No environment variables are currently required.
- SESSIONS store is in-memory only and process-local.
- uploads directory is created but file content is handled in memory.
- Treat README architecture as intent, not exact current filesystem truth.

## Cursor Behavior Guidance
- Prioritize minimal, surgical edits.
- Keep backend and frontend contracts synchronized.
- If changing data schema from API routes, update every dependent render function in dashboard.html within the same commit.
- Run a quick regression check of both backend mode and demo mode after modifications.
